  <content>
  <section>
    <section class="check-understanding">
      <exercise data-content-id="61773217-5b27-4b8b-bfca-abc27475c09f">
        <problem>
          <para>
      <para> The number of people with the flu during an epidemic is a function, \(f\), of the number of days, \(d\), since the epidemic began. The equation \(f(d)=50 \cdot (\frac{3}{2})^d\) defines \(f\).
          
          <para> How many people had the flu at the beginning of the epidemic? Do not enter commas or spaces in your answer.</para>
          </para>
      </para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>50</para>
          <para>
      <para>The correct answer is 50 because \(f(0)=50\).
      </para>
    </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </section>
</content>
